## Quarto

Quarto enables you to weave together content and executable code into a finished document. To learn more about Quarto see &lt;https://quarto.org&gt;.

## Running Code

When you click the **Render** button a document will be generated that includes both content and the output of embedded code. You can embed code like this:


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
1 + 1
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] 2
```


:::
:::


You can add options to executable code like this 


::: {.cell}
::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] 4
```


:::
:::


The `echo: false` option disables the printing of code (only output is displayed).

## Displaying code without rendering


```r
1+1
```

is not the same as 


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
1 + 1
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] 2
```


:::
:::


I can also do it in my markdown text where i know that 1+1=2.

